        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(agents): canonical agent creation with Custodian hatch flow",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\nAgent creation had three divergent implementations (gateway `agents.create` RPC, CLI `agents add`, and the Custodian's `create-agent` operation calling the CLI command function), with inconsistent workspace defaulting (`process.cwd()` on the gateway surface), no UI path to create an agent at all, and a hatch ceremony that only fired for first-run setup — a Custodian-created second agent got plain text and the client never learned the new agent's id.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\nOne canonical `createAgent` service now owns id validation/reservation, workspace defaulting, workspace+bootstrap seeding, identity write, and the exclusive config mutation; the RPC, CLI, and Custodian operation are thin wrappers (creation-path production LOC net flat). `agents.create`'s `workspace` becomes optional (additive) with server-side defaulting. The hatch ceremony now also fires for approved `create-agent` operations, and the chat result carries an additive `agentId` so clients can hand the user into the newborn agent's session with the \"Wake up, my friend!\" draft. The Control UI gains \"New agent\" entries (sidebar agent menu, agent picker footer, agents page) that open the Custodian with a server-owned `new-agent` welcome variant.\n\n## User Impact\nUsers can create agents from the UI through the same conversational, approval-gated Custodian flow used at first run, and land directly in the new agent's hatch. CLI and RPC behavior is unchanged except `workspace` is now optional on `agents.create`. No protocol version bump; all schema changes additive.\n\n## Evidence\n- Focused suites green (~361 tests): creation service, config-mutation exclusivity, CLI delegation, system-agent welcome/operations/chat-engine handoff, gateway mapping, UI custodian/route/picker suites.\n- Remote check-changed (format, typechecks, lint, boundary gates) green on Blacksmith Testbox.\n- Structured autoreview: clean, no actionable findings.\n",
